gui.ae2_qof.btn.upload=Upload Pattern\nAuto-upload the current encoded pattern to an interface/assembler on the network.\nShift+click forces the provider selection screen.
gui.ae2_qof.btn.recall=Recall Pattern\nTake back the last matching encoded pattern from the network.
gui.ae2_qof.btn.swap=Swap Outputs\nRotate primary/secondary output slot positions (Processing mode).
gui.ae2_qof.btn.matrix_upload=Upload to Matrix\nSend the encoded pattern to the GTNL Assembler Matrix library\n(Crafting mode + GTNL installed only).
gui.ae2_qof.btn.overlay=Overlay Toggle\nSwitch AE network count badges on NEI recipe pages/bookmarks.\nPure client-side setting, per player.
gui.ae2_qof.btn.halve=Halve Outputs\nDivide output amounts by 2 (spare key, currently hidden).
gui.ae2_qof.btn.wireless.add=Add Channel\nType a name then click to create a new global channel.
gui.ae2_qof.btn.wireless.remove=Remove Channel\nDelete the selected channel and tear down its connections.
gui.ae2_qof.btn.wireless.highlight=Highlight Links\nHighlight bound block positions of this channel in the world.\nToggle state is stored on this transceiver.
gui.ae2_qof.btn.wireless.sender=Set as Sender\nAct as the channel sender: register this transceiver on the channel.
gui.ae2_qof.btn.wireless.receiver=Set as Receiver\nAct as the channel receiver: connect to the sender of the channel.
gui.ae2_qof.btn.wireless.disconn=Disconnect\nTemporarily pause the current connection while keeping channel settings.

